<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Leuci</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 51 BCE (approx.) · capital Tullum</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Gallic people of southern Lorraine around Toul, steady suppliers of grain to Caesar's armies.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Leuci lived on the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moselle">Moselle</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meuse">Meuse</a>, in the modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">departments</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meurthe-et-moselle">Meurthe-et-Moselle</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vosges">Vosges</a>. Caesar mentions them among the peoples who supplied his army with grain in 58 BCE.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Nothing is known of their rulers. Their land included sanctuaries that grew important under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, above all Grand, a great healing shrine of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apollo-grannus">Apollo Grannus</a> with a large mosaic and amphitheatre.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The Leuci seem to have stayed loyal during the revolts, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> gave them the status of a free civitas. Their chief town <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toul">Tullum</a> became Toul, later one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/three-bishoprics">Three Bishoprics</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/leuci.jpg" alt="Leuci" width="320" height="325"><figcaption>Image: User:Feitscherg · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_Gallia_Tribes_Towns.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 51 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tullum</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gaulish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-176&amp;focus=leuci" aria-label="Leuci on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4816 477 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Leuci lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5136 733L5304 942"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5136 733h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5136 733h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Tullum. <a href="/atlas?year=-176&amp;focus=leuci">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

